it was n't the entire force , because there were still some who still had that lock-'em-up mentality , but there were other cops who saw the honor in partnering with the community , who saw the responsibility from themselves to be able to work as partners with community leaders and faith leaders in order to reduce violence in the community .
same with probation officers , same with judges , same with folks who were up that law enforcement chain , because they realized , like we did , that we 'll never arrest ourselves out of this situation , that there will not be enough prosecutions made , and you can not fill these jails up enough in order to alleviate the problem .
