now we 're also about to publish a study — the first study showing you can change gene expression in men with prostate cancer .
this is what 's called a heat map — and the different colors — and along the side , on the right , are different genes .
and we found that over 500 genes were favorably changed — in effect , turning on the good genes , the disease-preventing genes , turning off the disease-promoting genes .
and so these findings i think are really very powerful , giving many people new hope and new choices .
`` and companies like navigenics and dna direct and 23andme , that are giving you your genetic profiles , are giving some people a sense of , `` '' gosh , well , what can i do about it ? '' '' well , our genes are not our fate , and if we make these changes — they 're a predisposition — but if we make bigger changes than we might have made otherwise , we can actually change how our genes are expressed . ''
thank you .
